# API and Lib Structure

## API routes are feature-based
Each feature gets its own folder under `app/api/`:

```
app/api/
  brand-context/route.ts     ← GET + PATCH brand context
  outputs/route.ts           ← GET + POST outputs
  ai/
    generate/route.ts        ← POST generate content
    summarize/route.ts       ← POST summarize (future)
```

## Shared server logic goes in `lib/<domain>/`
```
lib/
  supabase/
    client.ts                ← browser Supabase client
    server.ts                ← server Supabase client (API routes)
  ai/
    prompts.ts               ← all prompts
    generate.ts              ← AI call logic
  types/
    database.ts              ← generated from Supabase schema
```

## Hard rules
- Never create a top-level `utils.ts` or `helpers.ts` catch-all file
- Never put shared logic directly inside a `route.ts` file — extract to `lib/`
- Never mix unrelated endpoints in the same folder
- If logic is used by more than one route, it belongs in `lib/`

## Adding a new endpoint
1. Create a feature folder under `app/api/`
2. Extract any reusable logic to `lib/<domain>/`
3. Keep `route.ts` thin — it handles HTTP, auth check, calls lib, returns response
